  "proof_admission": {
    "common_frame_invariant": "At label F write physical h=T_F*l. Serialized transition T_B*T_A^-1 preserves l; additions/copies at a common label, scales, and clears act exactly as their scalar events. Fresh both-orientation label checks and exact 800-column scalar identity therefore imply the full local physical identity on all external slices, not just the sampled e2e inputs.",
    "gauge_schedule": "Targets climb through nested entrance chains; centre private copies descend through served target levels (backward gather ascends), with paid child ranks at every transition, no unrelated climb while a copy is live, and explicit private clearing. All emitted common labels/endpoints and rank telescopes checked.",
    "normalization_and_owners": "Each of122entering helper complete chains is normalized by the two paid monomial wrappers to C_[w] tensor identity on all512basis columns. Complete-call all800owner injectivity ensures no other register touches its physical family during normalization. The residual and spectators extend to an explicit orthogonal73axis chart of the same owner. Disjoint residual slots across calls and untouched spectators permit the inherited whole-residual schedule.",
    "scope": "Finite witness under inherited all-size compiler, precision/tape/common-grid and analytic-transfer contracts. This audit does not discharge those contracts and does not claim an unconditional integer multiplication theorem.",
    "e2e_scope": "806basis and8dense inputs are direct program spot checks, not an exhaustive409600-column physical program matrix. Exhaustive local transition/normalizer identities plus all800scalar columns and the common-label proof give the all-input implication.",
    "overflow_scope": "Vendored post-operation int64 guards alone do not prove no wraparound. Independent Python-integer pre-operation bounds cover all expanding arithmetic in the executed operator/e2e audits, with maxima14and29bits.",
